+Requirements:
+1. `iadf/__init__.py` exposes `__version__ = "0.1.0"`.
+2. Each `*.schema.json` is a valid JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 document
+   with the exact `$id`, `$schema`, required properties, enums,
+   patterns, and `additionalProperties: false` constraints described
+   in the specification (mirrors ADD §4, §19.2, §20.2, §25.5). Pay
+   special attention to:
+   - the EXACT 11-value, EXACTLY-ordered `result` enum in
+     evidence_receipt.schema.json;
+   - nullable fields (`expires_at`, `binding_digest`, `activated_at`)
+     implemented via `"type": [<type>, "null"]` (and only applying
+     `pattern`/`format` constraints for the non-null branch, e.g. via
+     a `type` array on a single property definition — jsonschema
+     validators for `pattern`/`format` are simply skipped by the
+     jsonschema library when the instance is `null` and `type`
+     includes `"null"`, so a single property object with
+     `"type": ["string", "null"], "pattern": "..."` is sufficient and
+     correct);
+   - sha256 hex digest fields use `"pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"`;
+   - `data_residency` uses `"const": "eu-only"`;
+   - nested objects (`signature`, `budgets`, `rollback_contract`, and
+     each item of `change_set_plan`) all set
+     `"additionalProperties": false` and their own `required` lists.
+3. `iadf/schemas/__init__.py` implements:
+   - `RESULT_ALGEBRA`: tuple of the 11 result strings in the exact
+     order given in the spec.
+   - `SCHEMA_DIR`: `pathlib.Path` pointing at the directory containing
+     the schema files (i.e. `Path(__file__).parent`).
+   - `load_schema(name: str) -> dict`: maps `"evidence_receipt"`,
+     `"aoe"`, `"acm"` to their respective filenames, reads+parses the
+     JSON file, decorated with `functools.lru_cache`. Raises `KeyError`
+     for any other `name`.
+   - `class SchemaValidationError(Exception)`: stores `.errors` (a
+     list of strings) and a joined message.
+   - `validate_document(name: str, document: dict) -> None`: uses
+     `jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=jsonschema.FormatChecker())`,
+     collects ALL errors via `.iter_errors(document)`, builds one
+     human-readable string per error including the JSON path (e.g.
+     `"/".join(str(p) for p in error.absolute_path) or "<root>"` plus
+     `error.message`), and raises `SchemaValidationError(errors)` if
+     the list is non-empty; otherwise returns `None`.
