+1) FUNCTIONAL: `iadf/__init__.py` does not define `__version__`. Worse, the linter capsule reveals the file's content/path is corrupted by LLM prose leakage: ruff reports `N999 Invalid module name: 'Now produce final answer.iadf' --> Now produce final answer.iadf/__init__.py:1:1`. This means the previous generation step wrote a directory/file whose name embeds the model's chat preamble ("Now produce final answer."), i.e. the real `iadf/__init__.py` was created empty (hence `AttributeError: module 'iadf' has no attribute '__version__'`) while the intended content landed in a stray junk path. All 37 other tests pass, so the three schema JSON files and `iadf/schemas/__init__.py` are functionally correct; the only missing artefact is the one-line version marker.
+
+2) PROCESS: attempt 1 (aider) never produced a patch — it timed out at 600s (exit 124) after (a) trying to scrape https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema and install Playwright, and (b) entering a degenerate reasoning loop repeating "We'll also ensure `validate_document` uses `err.json_path`…" tens of thousands of times. The repair loop was destroyed by the model over-thinking the already-green schema/loader code and by URL auto-scraping triggered by the `$schema` literal in the prompt. Therefore the red test is still red for the same trivial reason as attempt 0.
+
+Conclusion: root cause = missing `__version__ = "0.1.0"` in `iadf/__init__.py` plus a stray non-importable junk file/dir named `Now produce final answer.iadf/` that pollutes lint. No schema or validator changes are needed.
