+- iadf/schemas/__init__.py
+- iadf/schemas/evidence_receipt.schema.json
+- iadf/schemas/aoe.schema.json
+- iadf/schemas/acm.schema.json
+
+Requirements recap:
+
+1. Each `.schema.json` file is a standalone JSON Schema Draft 2020-12
+   document (`"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"`)
+   with the exact `$id` values, required properties, enums (in the exact
+   order specified for `result`), patterns (`^[a-f0-9]{64}$` for all
+   sha256 digest fields), `additionalProperties: false` at every object
+   level described (including nested `budgets`, `signature`,
+   `rollback_contract`, and each item of `change_set_plan`), and the
+   exact literal values described in the specification (e.g.
+   `data_residency` const `"eu-only"`).
+
+2. `iadf/schemas/__init__.py` must expose:
+   - `RESULT_ALGEBRA`: an 11-tuple of strings, exact order:
+     PASS, FAIL, NOT_RUN, SKIPPED, UNKNOWN, ERROR, INCONCLUSIVE, TIMEOUT,
+     STALE, EXPIRED, SUPERSEDED.
+   - `SCHEMA_DIR`: a `pathlib.Path` pointing at the directory containing
+     the schema JSON files (i.e. `Path(__file__).parent`).
+   - `load_schema(name: str) -> dict` mapping `"evidence_receipt"`,
+     `"aoe"`, `"acm"` to their respective files, reading+`json.load`-ing
+     them, decorated with `functools.lru_cache`. Raise `KeyError` for any
+     other name (validate the name before hitting the cache, or let a
+     dict lookup raise KeyError naturally).
+   - `SchemaValidationError(Exception)`: stores `errors: list[str]` as an
+     attribute; `str()` should join them (e.g. with newlines) for useful
+     pytest output.
+   - `validate_document(name: str, document: dict) -> None`: build a
+     `jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=jsonschema.FormatChecker())`,
+     call `validator.iter_errors(document)`, and if any errors exist,
+     build one descriptive string per error (use `error.json_path` if
+     available, else `str(list(error.path))`, plus `error.message`) and
+     raise `SchemaValidationError(list_of_strings)`. Return `None` when
+     there are no errors.
+
+3. Use only the Python standard library (`json`, `functools`, `pathlib`)
+   plus the `jsonschema` package.
+
