+     keep it as the single source of truth.
+   - `SCHEMA_DIR` Path — already present, keep it.
+   - `load_schema(name: str) -> dict`: maps `"evidence_receipt"` ->
+     `evidence_receipt.schema.json`, `"aoe"` -> `aoe.schema.json`, `"acm"`
+     -> `acm.schema.json`; reads and JSON-parses the file from
+     `SCHEMA_DIR`; must raise `KeyError` for any other name; must be
+     wrapped with `functools.lru_cache`.
+   - `class SchemaValidationError(Exception)`: constructor takes a list of
+     error strings, stores it as `self.errors`, and calls
+     `super().__init__("; ".join(errors))`.
+   - `validate_document(name: str, document: dict) -> None`: THE
+     SIGNATURE ORDER IS `(name, document)`, NOT `(data, name)` as in the
+     current stub — this is a breaking fix required by the contract.
+     Load the schema via `load_schema(name)`, build a
+     `jsonschema.Draft202012Validator` with
+     `format_checker=jsonschema.FormatChecker()`, collect ALL validation
+     errors via `validator.iter_errors(document)`, format each as a
+     human-readable string that includes the JSON path (e.g. join
+     `error.absolute_path` with `/`), and if there is at least one error,
+     raise `SchemaValidationError(list_of_error_strings)`. Return `None`
+     silently if valid.
