+Requirements:
+1. `iadf/__init__.py` must expose `__version__ = "0.1.0"` (keep as-is).
+2. Author the three JSON Schema files exactly as specified (Draft 2020-12,
+   correct `$id`, `additionalProperties: false` at every nested object
+   level, exact enums/patterns/required lists as given). Pay special
+   attention to the EXACT 11-value ordered `result` enum in the evidence
+   receipt schema — this is a normative literal.
+3. Rewrite `iadf/schemas/__init__.py` to implement the real public API:
+   - `RESULT_ALGEBRA` tuple (11 values, exact order).
+   - `SCHEMA_DIR` = Path to this schemas directory.
+   - `load_schema(name: str) -> dict`: maps
+     `"evidence_receipt"->"evidence_receipt.schema.json"`,
+     `"aoe"->"aoe.schema.json"`, `"acm"->"acm.schema.json"`; reads and
+     `json.load`s the file; wrap with `functools.lru_cache`; raise
+     `KeyError` for any other name.
+   - `class SchemaValidationError(Exception)`: constructor takes a
+     `list[str]` and stores it as `self.errors`; also pass a joined
+     message to `super().__init__`.
+   - `validate_document(name: str, document: dict) -> None`: load schema
+     via `load_schema`, build
+     `jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=jsonschema.FormatChecker())`,
+     collect ALL errors via `.iter_errors(document)`, convert each to a
+     human-readable string that includes its JSON path (e.g.
+     `f"{'/'.join(str(p) for p in error.path) or '$'}: {error.message}"`),
+     and if the list is non-empty raise `SchemaValidationError(messages)`.
+     Return `None` if valid.
+4. Do not add any other public symbols that shadow these names, and do
+   not change the argument order of `validate_document` (name first,
+   document second) — tests depend on this exact signature.
